/target
# Cargo.lock IS TRACKED (2026-08-07, SPEC.RUST-BUILDER.CK.v3.11 §3).
# The shared builder reads the resolved pgrx version out of the crate's
# Cargo.lock and installs the exactly-matching cargo-pgrx. Untracked, a clean
# CI clone (§11) carries no lock to resolve from, and locally the lock is
# whatever that one machine last generated — which is how Cargo.toml drifted to
# ^0.16 while the on-disk lock held 0.19.2 without anything noticing.
*.so
*.dylib
.DS_Store
/.pgrx
*.swp
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# reference symlinks (local-only, not part of the repo)
/ref-*

/compose/extensions/pgrdf/
/compose/extensions/pgck/
/compose/pg-data/
/compose/dev-certs/
/fixtures/WIP/
/fixtures/
# local working docs/drafts; visible in the workspace, not tracked by git
/_WIP/

# Authoritative specs/roadmaps promoted to the workspace for working visibility, but the
# remote is the PUBLIC repo styk-tv/pgCK — anything starting with SPEC stays private
# (roadmap §15). Covers the v3.9 spec, the Critical-Isolation roadmap, the checklist, and any
# future SPEC.* drafts. No SPEC* file is tracked today, so this shadows nothing. Never commit.
SPEC*

# Playwright local test harness (install with `npm i` when needed; never tracked)
/node_modules/
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/.playwright-mcp/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
# Screenshot artifacts (MCP + page.screenshot) — home is tests/e2e/screenshots/, never tracked
/tests/e2e/screenshots/

# Python virtualenvs — never track (.venv was committed by mistake; untracked 2026-06-10)
/.venv/
.venv-dispatcher/
compose/extensions/pgck-natsclient/

# local env
.env

# VS Code tasks — local dev convenience, not shared (untracked 2026-07-28)
/.vscode/tasks.json

# CKP/SPEC statements and bench docs — never public (2026-08-05)
CK*.md
SPEC*.md

# bench scratch mount (nx5 REQ-3) — never tracked
.bench-scratch/
ontology.old/

# 2026-08-26 junk-scan hardening: classes that reached the public tree at
# 0.4.80/0.4.81 (removed same day found). drawio lock/backup files dodge the
# SPEC* glob via their .$ prefix; shell debris ('--', '-e') came from a
# mis-quoted command; archive drops of already-tracked trees are never source.
.$*
*.bkp
*.drawio.bkp
ConceptKernel*-ontologies.zip
__MACOSX/
--
-e

# 2026-08-26: web/ leaves this repo's tracked tree (operator ruling — pgck-web
# will not be carried here; working tree kept for the bench bind-mounts, history
# untouched). Python bytecode litter ignored with it.
web/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
tests/doc-conflict-resolution/
